==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
Uncertain. Possibly related to {{cog|it|puttana}} ({{cog|osp|putaña}}; see {{m|es|putañear}}), which ultimately derives from {{der|pt|la|putus|t=boy}}. María Moliner dictionary (also Joan Coromines<ref>[[w:en:Joan Coromines|Joan Coromines]], ''Breve diccionario etimológico de la lengua castellana'', tercera edición 2011, {{ISBN|978-84-249-0374-9}}</ref>) states the most probable origin: from {{der|pt|VL.|putta}}, variant of {{m|la|puta}}, female form of {{m|la|puttus}}, {{m|la|putus|t=boy}}. Note that this word appears in all Romance languages.

===Noun===
{{pt-noun|f}}

# {{lb|pt|vulgar|pejorative}} {{l|en|prostitute}}, {{l|en|whore}}, {{l|en|hooker}}, {{l|en|slut}}

===Adjective===
{{pt-adj|f}}

# {{adj form of|pt|puto||f|s}}
# {{lb|pt|vulgar|pejorative|of a girl or woman}} {{l|en|promiscuous}}
# {{lb|pt|only in some cities in|_|Brazil|vulgar|also in Portugal}} an [[intensifier]] used in a similar way as [[fucking]], [[frigging]] or [[damn]] may be used in the USA. May mean "huge", "impressive" and/or "problematic" and can even be used in a good way if the person is jealous
#: {{syn|pt|baita|gaita}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não pude ir lá por causa de uma '''puta''' tempestade.|inline=1|I could not go there, because of a fucking storm.}}
#: {{ux|pt|Você tem uma '''puta''' sorte.|inline=1|You're so frigging lucky.}}

